.TH TEE 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
tee \- read from standard input and write to standard output and files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tee
[\fB\-a\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy standard input to standard output and to each FILE.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-append
Append to FILE(s) instead of overwriting them.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 if a FILE could not be opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
